Reach other nodes' agents over HTTP through the gRPC CONNECT proxy.

With RAY_grpc_enable_http_proxy set, the head reaches other nodes' raylets and
agents over gRPC through the HTTP CONNECT proxy named by grpc_proxy,
https_proxy, or http_proxy. The dashboard's HTTP calls to the same agents do
not: the State API's runtime env query and the job head's calls to the job
agent open plain aiohttp sessions, so a worker that only the proxy can reach,
such as one on remote capacity behind a tunnel, cannot answer `ray list
runtime-envs` or the job submissions and log reads routed to its agent. The new
NodeAgentConnector makes both sessions follow the same proxy choice as gRPC,
including no_grpc_proxy (or no_proxy when it is unset), and tunnels each
proxied connection with CONNECT. Without the gRPC proxy flag, nothing changes.

Upstream status: not yet reported to ray-project/ray.

